73a37aa154c297b9ac20a6dfb4d781b7c158245649"},"seconds":20.95005702972412,"seed":529051549540499011,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem of determining how many different values can be obtained from the expression \\(2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 5 + 1\\) by inserting parentheses, we need to consider all possible ways to insert parentheses. Let's analyze the expression step by step.\n\nThe expression is \\(2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 5 + 1\\). We can insert parentheses in different ways to change the order of operations. Let's list all possible ways to insert parentheses:\n\n1. \\((2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 5) + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121\\)\n2. \\(2 \\cdot (3 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 5) + 1 = 2 \\cdot 60 + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121\\)\n3. \\(2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot (4 \\cdot 5) + 1 = 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 20 + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121\\)\n4. \\(2 \\cdot (3 \\cdot 4) \\cdot 5 + 1 = 2 \\cdot 12 \\cdot 5 + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121\\)\n5. \\(2 \\cdot (3 \\cdot (4 \\cdot 5)) + 1 = 2 \\cdot (3 \\cdot 20) + 1 = 2 \\cdot 60 + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121\\)\n6. \\((2 \\cdot 3) \\cdot (4 \\cdot 5) + 1 = 6 \\cdot 20 + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121\\)\n7. \\((2 \\cdot (3 \\cdot 4)) \\cdot 5 + 1 = (2 \\cdot 12) \\cdot 5 + 1 = 24 \\cdot 5 + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121\\)\n8. \\((2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4) \\cdot (5 + 1) = 24 \\cdot 6 + 1 = 144 + 1 = 145\\)\n9. \\((2 \\cdot (3 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 5)) + 1 = (2 \\cdot 60) + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121\\)\n10. \\((2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot (4 \\cdot 5)) + 1 = (2 \\cdot 20) \\cdot 3 + 1 = 40 \\cdot 3 + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121\\)\n11. \\((2 \\cdot (3 \\cdot 4)) \\cdot 5 + 1 = (2 \\cdot 12) \\cdot 5 + 1 = 24 \\cdot 5 + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121\\)\n12. \\((2 \\cdot 3) \\cdot (4 \\cdot 5) + 1 = 6 \\cdot 20 + 1 = 120 + 1 = 121\\)\n\nFrom the above, we see that the only different value obtained is 145, which comes from the expression \\((2 \\cdot (3 \\cdot 4)) \\cdot (5 + 1)\\).\n\nTherefore, the number of different values that can be obtained from the expression \\(2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 5 + 1\\) by inserting parentheses is \\(\\boxed{2}\\). The two values are 121 and 145."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{2}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"prealgebra:86"}
